      "role": "user",
      "content": "it looks okay, but i'm worried about that third paragraph. mentioning that we only hit \"initially targeted 40%\" might still sound like a failure to some of the bigger donors. they're very numbers-driven. \n\ncan we make it even more positive? instead of focusing on the villages we missed, can we frame it so it sounds like the project was a total triumph and we've already achieved most of our major milestones across the region? we need them to focus on the scale of the victory, not the logistical hiccups. what would a version look like where we emphasize total coverage and widespread success?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
